I regenerated the two quantitative figures. The overview schematic's warnings are still open. `paper.tex` recompiles cleanly to 13 pages, the same count as before. I didn't re-run the validator, so I haven't confirmed the warnings are gone.

- **Font sizes:** In `scripts/build_figures.py` I raised the title font to 10 pt and the axis-label font to 9 pt. I also moved the "reference = 1" label in panel (a) so it no longer runs over the plot frame. I updated those font sizes in `figure_manifest.json` for the two matplotlib figures.
- **PNG width:** The PNG exports are now 2420 px wide, up from 1650. I got there by raising the PNG export to 440 DPI instead of 300, because 300 DPI on a 5.5 in figure only gives 1650 px.
- **PDF links:** `paper.tex` already referenced the vector PDFs for both figures, so no relinking was needed.
